SOAPBOX: I had decided this year to enter the Classic section, for various reasons.
SOAPBOX: I traveled on the Wednesday before CQWW, and was aware that there were some antenna maintenance to perform beforehand, as well as the usual winding up of the towers, and putting out the LF antennae.
SOAPBOX: The weather was not friendly on arrival, and we had to do the work on Thursday, that was a wonderful Day. The weather forecast warned of 2 named storms coming through and we curtailed the height of our towers to take this into account.
SOAPBOX: The forecast didn't disappoint right from the off I was on the back foot:
SOAPBOX: - the Quad band beam suddenly developed higher SWR from the Saturday morning I think it was due to water. On Saturday night, the beam detached itself from the tower, and in the morning I found it suspended by the support wires.
SOAPBOX: - the main tribander also developed a fault the winds had loosened the beam clamp, in turn allowing it to freewheel, and ripped out the support wire, now dancing on the elements with the storm
SOAPBOX: - thankfully the 3rd beam was intact as were the LF dipoles
SOAPBOX: The whole plan was compromised by the disasters!
SOAPBOX: 10m never played well and 40m was hard on the 1st night.
SOAPBOX: We will be going somewhere warm for CW!
